    "## Question\n",
    "\n",
    "**Question.** How well does Friday's archived NOAA NBM forecast estimate whether the CoCoRaHS 24-hour report following a Saturday records at least 0.01 inches of rain at station VA-FX-121?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Quantity.** Probability (0-1) that the next-morning CoCoRaHS report totals at least 0.01 inches. The Saturday 7-9 p.m. yoga class is the setting and decision context; class-hour rain is not the quantity being predicted. The canopy rule uses the probability of a wet daily report, as agreed with the professor. The report is only a proxy for rain during class.\n"
   ]
  },
