    "## Data\n",
    "\n",
    "Each row is a candidate Saturday. The outcome is the next-morning 24-hour report at CoCoRaHS station VA-FX-121, Fairfax 3.2 W. Forecast inputs are two NBM NBE P12 probabilities for KIAD, issued Friday at 13Z, for 12-hour windows ending Sunday 00Z and 12Z. The forecast station is about 14 km from the gauge. The gauge is generally read around 7 a.m.; its window is about one hour offset from the paired forecast windows and includes rain outside the 7-9 p.m. class.\n",
    "\n",
    "For the chosen target, the daily amount is the outcome itself. If we instead claimed to predict class-hour rain, a wet daily report caused by rain at other hours would create false-positive labels; that time-window mismatch is systematic, not a residual to be absorbed. The airport-to-gauge difference and variable report time add further measurement noise. Do not interpret the model probability as class-hour rain probability.\n",
    "\n",
    "data/README.md documents sources, terms, reconstruction, and the SHA-256 checked above. The raw plot and summary table below precede modeling.\n"
   ]
